        "PMC10774414::web::004::dual_gradient_ptfeconicu_hea_model",
        "PMC10288253::web::022::discussion_effect_of_heo_composition_on_"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A downward d-band-center shift will weaken the adsorption of poisoning ethanol-oxidation intermediates.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Weaker adsorption of reaction intermediates can promote catalytic performance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10774414::web::004::dual_gradient_ptfeconicu_hea_model",
        "PMC10774414::web::007::gaussian_distribution_of_gh_on_ptfeconic"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Weaker binding of poisoning intermediates will reduce surface poisoning.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced surface poisoning will facilitate faster catalytic turnover.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Pt-reduced, Rh-enriched catalysts will exhibit a lower ethanol-oxidation onset potential than the equimolar catalyst.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Pt-reduced, Rh-enriched catalysts will exhibit a higher turnover frequency than the equimolar catalyst.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Pt-reduced, Rh-enriched catalysts will exhibit enhanced durability relative to the equimolar catalyst.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-entropy alloy nanoparticles can retain catalytic activity and alloy homogeneity during prolonged operation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6728353::web::010::catalytic_studies_for_ammonia_decomposit"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The composition-induced electronic shift can be monitored in situ using XAS or XPS.",
